## 1. CLI Side: Where Slash Commands Are Defined (Python)

### Core registry class
**`src/consilium/utils/slashcmd.py`** — Defines `SlashCommand` dataclass and `SlashCommandRegistry`. The registry maps command names and aliases to functions. Key methods:
- `command()` — decorator to register a command (with optional `name` and `aliases`)
- `find_command(name)` — look up by name or alias
- `list_commands()` — return all unique primary commands

### Three separate registries

| Registry | File | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `soul_slash_registry` | `src/consilium/soul/slash.py` | Commands executed by `ConsiliumSoul.run()` |
| `shell_slash_registry` | `src/consilium/ui/shell/slash.py` | Commands executed by `Shell` UI (may trigger reloads, open windows, etc.) |
| `shell_mode_registry` | `src/consilium/ui/shell/slash.py` | Subset of shell commands available in **shell mode** (non-agent) |
| `think_registry` | `src/consilium/think/slash.py` | Commands for Think mode sessions |

### Soul-level commands (`soul/slash.py`) — **these are sent to the CLI agent**

| Command | Aliases | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/init` | — | Analyze the codebase and generate `AGENTS.md` |
| `/compact` | — | Compact context (optionally with focus instruction) |
| `/clear` | `reset` | Clear the context |
| `/yolo` | — | Toggle YOLO mode (auto-approve all actions) |
| `/afk` | — | Toggle AFK mode (auto-dismiss questions, auto-approve) |
| `/plan` | — | Toggle plan mode; subcommands: `on`, `off`, `view`, `clear` |
| `/add-dir` | — | Add a directory to the workspace |
| `/export` | — | Export current session context to markdown |
| `/import` | — | Import context from a file or session ID |
| `/commit` | — | Create intermediate git commit (Do mode) |
| `/abort` | — | Abort session and revert to initial git state (Do mode) |
| `/status` | — | Show git status (Do mode) |
| `/complete` | — | Mark current phase complete (Do mode) |
| `/inject` | — | Inject a message into context (Do mode) |
| `/skill:<name>` | — | Run a skill (dynamically registered) |
| `/flow:<name>` | — | Run a prompt flow (dynamically registered) |

